  "id": "COMPOUND:33280 - PROTEIN:5794",
  "verbalization": "Sarcotrine A is shown to have a target relationship with LAPC4 through multiple indirect pathways. The first pathway links Sarcotrine A to Raji, which is targeted by a complex compound that ultimately targets LAPC4. The second pathway connects Sarcotrine A to Hepatocyte, which is targeted by 5-Hydroxy-6,8-Dimethoxy-2,3-Dimethylbenzo[G]Chromen-4-One, which also targets LAPC4. The third pathway similarly links Sarcotrine A to Hepatocyte, which is targeted by Cocosamide B, which also targets LAPC4. These pathways collectively suggest that Sarcotrine A may act through a shared target, LAPC4, via different intermediates. The evidence supports a potential mechanism where Sarcotrine A influences LAPC4 through various downstream targets, highlighting a possible dependency on these intermediates. The integration of these pathways underscores the role of LAPC4 as a central node in the signaling network influenced by Sarcotrine A.",
